{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions","id":45674,"title":"Beastmen? How about Plantmen, Fungusmen, or Virusmen? - Lunar questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-09T09:57:34-08:00","id":45674,"title":"Beastmen? How about Plantmen, Fungusmen, or Virusmen? - Lunar questions","content":"The Knack <i>Laurels-and-Ivy Technique</i> allows a Lunar to &quot;assume the shapes of plants and other non-animal life&quot; (see <b>Manual of Exalted Power - Lunars</b>, page 134). I am going to go out on a limb here and say that other non-animal, non-supernatural life refers to various kind of fungi or possibly vira if there exists a Knack that goes smaller than <i>Emerald Grasshopper Form</i> (see <b>Manual of Exalted Power - Lunars</b>, page 131) and if it is not assumed the vira do not exist because disease gods exist instead.<br /> <br /> That is cool, but the downside of turning into a plant, fungus, or vira is that you are Inactive, meaning that you can take no actions (see <b>Exalted </b>page 143).<br /> <br /> Would it be fair to assume, you think, that there exists an upgrade to this Knack allowing the Lunar to take actions? Or is a Lunar in that shape limited to Reflexive Charms which magical beings may activate &quot;on any tick, whether or not they have an action that tick&quot; (see <b>Exalted </b>page 142)?<br /> <br /> Now, upon concieving a child, the Stamina Charm <i>Fish or Fowl Gestation </i>allows the Lunar to &quot;imprint the child with features from any shape in her Heart\u2019s Blood library, including her spirit shape, rather than being restricted to the form she currently wears&quot; (see <b>Glories of the Most High - Luna</b>, page 23). I am assuming that this means that the Lunar my concieve Plantmen or Fungusmen if she has plants or fungi in her Heart's Blood Library.<br /> <br /> Would you allow this? Why or why not?<br /> <br /> And how about Virusmen? Could that be a thing, theoretically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T10:02:01-08:00","id":45676,"title":"","content":"Well, &quot;viruses&quot; aren't really a thing in Creation, so I don't think so. That would be a demonblood or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T10:02:38-08:00","id":45678,"title":"","content":"Chakra Orchid all up in this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T10:11:25-08:00","id":45684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions#post45674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you allow this? Why or why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally, because it seems cool. Generally, though, I think I would want their vegetative traits to be subtler than the animal traits of a beastman. Less piney, more <i>vishakanya</i> or ent.<br /> <br /> No virusmen, though, because I figure that Creation tends toward less scientific reasons for disease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T10:11:33-08:00","id":45685,"title":"","content":"Plant and fungi would be fine. Viruses aren't a form of life and don't exist in Creation, as far as we know.<br /> <br /> I wonder if <i>Laurels-and-Ivy Technique</i> would let a PC be a Cylon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T10:19:41-08:00","id":45687,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd leave out viruses, as I don't think even the Lunar definition of &quot;life&quot; is quite that permissive, but change that to &quot;protozoa&quot; and you're back in business. Also, I don't think we can say Creation doesn't have pathogens like viruses; just because diseases are overseen by disease spirits doesn't mean there isn't a physical vector that does the transmission; that's kind of like saying there are no fungi because there are gods that oversee decomposition.<br /> <br /> All that said, yeah, totally breed plant-men, fungus men, whatever. Anywhere from subtle barky skin to the pineys from Compass: Wyld. The more interesting question is, what kind of Lunar would do this, and why?<br /> <br /> I'd probably draw the line at protozoa, because how would you even go about melding a single-cell lifeform with a human? But anything &quot;above&quot; that, sure!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 01-09-2014, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T10:33:13-08:00","id":45702,"title":"","content":"I dunno. At least with animals, there is a certain amount of sese to being able to reproduce. Sperm fertilizes eggs. Your Lunar sprouts flowers and germinates seeds is just... I dunno. It is somehow lacking in vigor.<br /> <br /> I don't want to fall into the trap of Lunars being the animal exalted, but I think them being the 'breeding exalted' is an even more vile trap.<br /> <br /> Besides, who wants to walk into a cloud of pollen and give birth to a baby dandelion girl a year later?<br /> <br /> There needs to be some sort of boundary nd the the kingdom of Anamalia seems like about enough to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1199-mister-lion","name":"Mister Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T11:19:09-08:00","id":45724,"title":"","content":"Yes, except for viruses. I'm not sure Lunars can can go sub-cellular (and if there is any meaningful distinction between a bacteria and a virus for them).<br /> <br /> There's an Abomination that's very useful for describing such a thing - that one that transforms you into nothing but a bag of flesh filled with bugs. I don't see why a Lunar couldn't birth *-men which count as having that mutation for representing their swarm-of-bacteria / mass-of-fungus bodies. It might need to be tweaked a little to fit.<br /> <br /> I also don't see problem with giving birth to Ents or Dryads (except any that would arise through birth complications involving branches).<br /> <br /> Also, since it &quot;imprints features&quot; onto the child, it doesn't need to be a person <i>made</i> of a disease, it could be a permanent carrier that has a symbiotic relationship with the disease, and it doesn't need to be a humanoid plant so much as a person with the Leaves mutation or a fungus equivalent (though take that enough times and you're more plant than human anyway).<br /> <br /> Basically, it all comes down to being able to model it with mutation points (including custom ones) that wouldn't count as Wyld Mutations (for deciding survivability and viability in Creation, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-09-2014, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T11:55:47-08:00","id":45746,"title":"","content":"Ents, Dryads, Treefolk!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T12:20:50-08:00","id":45760,"title":"","content":"Beastmen stem from tales like that of the Minotaur, Cynocephali, or goat-men. The body of lore that involves anthropomorphic plants, in contrast, tends to make them poor PC material, since it includes the Jinmenju (human-faced tree) and folklore about the mandrake root shape. So they'd still be stuck in the ground, living and growing in the way that plants do, save for legends that seem better placed with other Exalted, such as vampire pumpkins and watermelons (beware the Abyssal farmer!) or ganja-smoking tree people/demons from the Phillipines.<br /> <br /> So I'd say, let another variety of Exalt take care of the hybrids that aren't two animals. The Lunars have a connection to Gaia through animals, as wild-running hunters, rather than through any form of life that they can't take as a spirit shape under any circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T12:38:52-08:00","id":45775,"title":"","content":"Honestly? I'm totally okay with the concept of Lunars creating plant-people.<br /> <br /> ... mostly because it has the potential for some really really cute characters. Though, admittedly, it does open up more stories - say, a Lunar creating a society where those blessed with the forms of life-giving trees (ones that grow food, like apples) are viewed as divine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T14:16:54-08:00","id":45846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=45775#post45775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, admittedly, it does open up more stories - say, a Lunar creating a society where those blessed with the forms of life-giving trees (ones that grow food, like apples) are viewed as divine.</div> </div> </div> </div>One Immaculate Fire Aspect later...<br /> <br /> Or alternately, sneak in Fire DB blood and wait for some of the descendants to Exalt.<br /> <br /> Granted, the society would probably highly select toward Wood DBs instead. Though, could Wood DB animas partially control nearby plantpeople as a stunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/240-winged-cat","name":"Winged Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar240_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T14:25:56-08:00","id":45848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Winged Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=45846#post45846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or alternately, sneak in Fire DB blood and wait for some of the descendants to Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it might be kind of distressing -- esp. the actual moment of Exaltation -- I dunno if this would quite work as sabotage. Terrestrials are immune to the hazards of their animas, as I recall. They might wind up seeming even more deified. Burning bush men!<br /> <br /> EDIT: If viewed as holy, they <i>would</i> probably -- reverently but firmly -- be made to live apart from the rest of society, granted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 01-09-2014, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T15:29:09-08:00","id":45884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Winged Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=45846#post45846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though, could Wood DB animas partially control nearby plantpeople as a stunt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Were I ruling on that situation myself, I'd say &quot;no.&quot; That just creates too many problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T22:40:46-08:00","id":46085,"title":"","content":"&quot;roll the dice to see if the ebola wants to sleep with me!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T08:38:18-08:00","id":46281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=46085#post46085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;roll the dice to see if the ebola wants to sleep with me!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah! Talk about the Hot Zone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T14:52:24-08:00","id":46518,"title":"","content":"Exalted clearly has something resembling germ theory, because they have a far better understanding of sterilization than we did at their technology level, but I'm not sure actual individual germs exist in Creation, and if they do it's probably not something you'd want to lampshade. If you want to talk real-world science I'm not sure a virus would count as an organism in the first place, but even if you shift it to bacteria I don't think &quot;prokaryote form&quot; is really a place you want to go. IMO, the fact that Exalted tends to steer well clear of talking about microorganisms is evidence enough that if you go that way you're invoking Rule Zero. I think you could theoretically justify having a Lunar turn into a contagion or illness (in aggregate), because that lies somewhere in the confluence of the plant knack and Air Body, but I wouldn't allow it personally.<br /> <br /> I would actually probably houserule the &quot;always inactive rule&quot; as it stands, because I don't see why you shouldn't be able to perform any actions that don't require movement. That said, I think a followup power to let you move is reasonable. I'd probably require mote-spend and commitment for it, but I'd certainly allow it.<br /> <br /> I would absolutely allow a lunar to sire plantmen and fungusmen with the powers you describe, because it seems in-theme, and what's the harm? Those powers suck, so a player who takes them is clearly really in love with the gimmick. However, since beastmen are fundamentally human, I'd rule that they're still animals who have some of the properties and appearance of plants/fungus, rather than being Swamp Thing. I imagine there's an unwritten followup to that power that lets you just sire outright Weird Monsters, though.<br /> <br /> I always liked the idea of a Lunar who combined the plant-shape Knack and the Leviathan form to go into deep cover as a mycelium bed in a forest. They wouldn't be able to change form without spending a day doing it and destroying the forest in the process, but I figured they would have some &quot;municipal charm&quot; type effects for manipulating the forest, and could communicate with agents through spores and mushroom patterns. Even that's getting really abstract for a Lunar, but I like the idea on its own merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 01-10-2014, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T15:41:00-08:00","id":46551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister Lion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=45702#post45702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, who wants to walk into a cloud of pollen and give birth to a baby dandelion girl a year later?</div> </div> </div> </div>... I have my next Exalted character. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T16:14:50-08:00","id":46574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrivYeti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=46551#post46551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... I have my next Exalted character. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inspired too. Would God-blood or Lunar Half-Caste be better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T00:43:40-08:00","id":46781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wingnut2292</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=46574#post46574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm inspired too. Would God-blood or Lunar Half-Caste be better?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would depend on whether the child inherited her parent's powers or if they became a beastman, but I don't know what causes the difference.<br /> <br /> Also, I full heartedly support the idea of a plantman tribe somewhere in the reaches of Creation, Pinemen to the North, the Kelpkin in the West, things in the East that are half-Vine and half-human and a nation of Cactus folk that have hair of spines. But I ramble, the idea of a race of people who are part plant would be interesting.<br /> I wonder if they could do photosynthesis of light to feed themselves. But I'm not sure if there is any advantage for a Lunar to breed plantmen or fungimen. Probably only bred as a curiousity or specialist servant if the plantmen would have specialist powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T01:20:34-08:00","id":46787,"title":"","content":"I am impressed by how many people are actually open to this idea and willing to discuss it.<br /> <br /> Looking at the Blight <i>Acidic Pustules </i>(see <b>Manual of Exalted Power - Lunars</b>, page 208), it is pretty hardcore. For every point of damage you suffer, you roll an equal number of damage dice for everyone within five yards. I do not think that it would break anything to replace the acid splash with exposure to a toxin as per the <i>Toxin </i>Affliction (see <b>Exalted</b>, page 289) and keep it as a Blight called <i>Spores</i>.<br /> <br /> Now, whenever you take damage, a cloud of poisonous fungus spores erupt from you. If I were an unscrupulous Lunar, I would see a lot of potential in breeding an army of poisonous fungusmen.<br /> <br /> The virusmen would probably be mimicked most easily with the Deformity <i>Plague Carrier </i>(see <b>Exalted</b>, page 290).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T17:14:32-08:00","id":47138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=46781#post46781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if they could do photosynthesis of light to feed themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeeh. Correct me if I'm wrong, but I would say the energy requirements of a stationary plant are pretty trivial compared to the constant need of an animal to fuel its brain, heart, lungs and other important organs, not to mention, you know, moving around and doing stuff. It might make you a bit more energetic with access to the sun, but it wouldn't make for a complete replacement of food.<br /> <br /> Also, people tend to think of photosynthesis as this magical sunlight-to-life thing, but it doesn't stop you from needing nutrients. So even if a plantman could use photosynthesis for all of its energy needs, being mostly human, it would still need vitamins and proteins and all kinds of things... which means eating meat and fruit, etc. Or eating dirt, I suppose, if we're going for a mostly plant being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T20:29:49-08:00","id":47219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47138#post47138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eeeeh. Correct me if I'm wrong, but I would say the energy requirements of a stationary plant are pretty trivial compared to the constant need of an animal to fuel its brain, heart, lungs and other important organs, not to mention, you know, moving around and doing stuff. It might make you a bit more energetic with access to the sun, but it wouldn't make for a complete replacement of food.<br /> <br /> Also, people tend to think of photosynthesis as this magical sunlight-to-life thing, but it doesn't stop you from needing nutrients. So even if a plantman could use photosynthesis for all of its energy needs, being mostly human, it would still need vitamins and proteins and all kinds of things... which means eating meat and fruit, etc. Or eating dirt, I suppose, if we're going for a mostly plant being.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's essentially the issue at hand. You'd also need to drink three or more times your normal amount of water every day, not wear clothes, and not actually stand motionless in the sun, because that might burn out your thylakoids (there's a reason that plants tilt their leaves during the day), and during hot weather, there's a high probability that you might undergo photorespiration, which eliminates your stores of sugar with no energy benefit if you don't use the C4 or CAM systems of carbon-fixation... which are more energy-intensive than normal, photorespiration-vulnerable C3 (predictably enough, the C# format indicates how many carbons the resulting sugars have. CAM indicates that a system of acid production is instituted instead.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T00:26:14-08:00","id":47283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47219#post47219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that's essentially the issue at hand. You'd also need to drink three or more times your normal amount of water every day, not wear clothes, and not actually stand motionless in the sun, because that might burn out your thylakoids (there's a reason that plants tilt their leaves during the day), and during hot weather, there's a high probability that you might undergo photorespiration, which eliminates your stores of sugar with no energy benefit if you don't use the C4 or CAM systems of carbon-fixation... which are more energy-intensive than normal, photorespiration-vulnerable C3 (predictably enough, the C# format indicates how many carbons the resulting sugars have. CAM indicates that a system of acid production is instituted instead.)</div> </div> </div> </div>All true, of course - except in Exalted, there's no such thing as photorespiration, thylakoids, carbon-fixation, and so on.<br /> <br /> Wood is a fundamental essence of the world, a base unit of matter which shows the properties of real-life plants without truly being identical to them. Plants grow because it is the nature of Wood to grow or gain energy from sunlight, not because light is a key part of carbon fixation.<br /> <br /> I would be hesitant to make Plantmen completely reliant on food rather than sunlight, but making them able to, say, eat once a week or whatever should be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1022-tzar1990","name":"tzar1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T05:50:03-08:00","id":47333,"title":"","content":"I am so very much having my players encounter a small tribe of what looks like this next they delve into the eastern jungles:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://1-media-cdn.foolz.us/ffuuka/board/tg/image/1345/89/1345897485009.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T06:17:09-08:00","id":47342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tzar1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47283#post47283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All true, of course - except in Exalted, there's no such thing as photorespiration, thylakoids, carbon-fixation, and so on.<br /> <br /> Wood is a fundamental essence of the world, a base unit of matter which shows the properties of real-life plants without truly being identical to them. Plants grow because it is the nature of Wood to grow or gain energy from sunlight, not because light is a key part of carbon fixation.<br /> <br /> I would be hesitant to make Plantmen completely reliant on food rather than sunlight, but making them able to, say, eat once a week or whatever should be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>But plants in Creation still need water and fertile soil, and humans in Creation still need a diverse alimentation to stay healthy. That they use magical rather than chemical processes doesn't change that the requirements for life are essentially the same as in RL.<br /> <br /> It doesn't make sense for a simple Lunar-born plantman to actually be better at it than a normal plant, so the need for water, nutrients and avoiding getting sunburned would remain the same, even if the plantman doesn't literally have thylakoids. Now, if we were talking about an actually magical being with Wood-themed powers, like a god-blood or Exigent or whatever (can elementals make god-bloods?), I would be more open to the idea of letting it break the normal limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T06:18:08-08:00","id":47343,"title":"","content":"\u2026and unless your players are particularly exceptionally mature, you might have to mentally prepare yourself for all the dick-jokes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T08:16:07-08:00","id":47396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tzar1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47283#post47283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All true, of course - except in Exalted, there's no such thing as photorespiration, thylakoids, carbon-fixation, and so on.<br /> <br /> Wood is a fundamental essence of the world, a base unit of matter which shows the properties of real-life plants without truly being identical to them. Plants grow because it is the nature of Wood to grow or gain energy from sunlight, not because light is a key part of carbon fixation.<br /> <br /> I would be hesitant to make Plantmen completely reliant on food rather than sunlight, but making them able to, say, eat once a week or whatever should be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read through the Wood Aspect book? There's a section in it on cellular metabolism. It indicates that there's more to it than you're suggesting. Additionally, your metaphysics are slightly confused. Wood is the element representing all life, not just plants. It also works as a process, rather than in any detail. And the details still remain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T08:55:22-08:00","id":47412,"title":"","content":"Well let's be honest, the only reason beastmen were included in the first place was to pander to furries who get off on bestiality. I am STILL ashamed for white wolf for going full retard on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1646-finch181","name":"finch181","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T11:51:52-08:00","id":47517,"title":"","content":"I don't know where this &quot;In Creation there's no such thing as medical science as we know it&quot; thing comes from. Check the description of the snakemen biology in Castebook... Night, was it? Cell division.<br /> <br /> Germs and viruses and things are all happening behind the scenes; people understand them in different terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T12:08:39-08:00","id":47534,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I like Creation's medical stuff working the same way as ours, with the spiritual side as an add-on rather than a replacement. It makes Creation more intuitive for players portraying characters who've always lived there. Sure, you should be able to treat Malaria by doing a ritual and praying to the Mosquito-Goddess...but the ritual involves brewing the bark of a tree to make a potion of sacred quinine water, most of the time. I don't want you to be able to cure a plague by calling up the plague-god and beating him up, and I don't think treating individual patients should look like an exorcism (most of the time-supernatural diseases like Green Sun Wasting or the Contagion might be different). I want it to involve steaming cups of herbal teas and wrapping patients in prayer strips soaked in water from a sacred fountain or ritualized bloodletting or acupuncture. I want my Exalted Healer characters to feel like doctors, not just magic away the problem.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with using mystical forces to weaken the sickness and oppose its spread and strengthen the patient so he/she can fight off infection, and I'm fine with spirits inflicting illnesses as a curse or punishment as an additional vector for the disease...but I want dealing with spirits and magical energies to be a thing where you increase or decrease the odds of survival/infection, not something that cures/inflicts the condition, y'know?<br /> <br /> Anyway, back on topic? Pretty sure Lunar &quot;I am super-attractive charms&quot; plus changing into plants can lead to pregnant trees. Good way to seduce forest-gods or wood-elementals in particular, I feel, might make a nice backstory for a godblooded character. Being born from a tree is a nice mythic sorta backstory for a character. Sorta Monkey King-ish. I'm probably more comfortable with tribes of humanoids with plant-features being the result of patronage by forest spirits or wood elementals and lots of godbloods over many generations, but I could see Lunars doing this as a one-off trick. Wouldn't want to make it a character's whole schtick though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T12:15:28-08:00","id":47542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47517#post47517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know where this &quot;In Creation there's no such thing as medical science as we know it&quot; thing comes from. Check the description of the snakemen biology in Castebook... Night, was it? Cell division.<br /> <br /> Germs and viruses and things are all happening behind the scenes; people understand them in different terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ex2 disease descriptions, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T12:49:43-08:00","id":47561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47542#post47542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ex2 disease descriptions, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beat me to it.<br /> <br /> Cholera can come from letting criminals bathe in open water sources, and hysteria can be fought off with resistance rolls, though Contagion-Curing Touch can't stop it. While most of what's in there is clearly true from modern knowledge through an ancient-world lens, but there's enough there that clearly isn't to muddy the waters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T13:19:33-08:00","id":47577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47517#post47517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know where this &quot;In Creation there's no such thing as medical science as we know it&quot; thing comes from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like thinking of things in terms of symbolism rather than practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T14:18:42-08:00","id":47601,"title":"","content":"&quot;Only stuff visible to the naked eye matches our modern knowledge base&quot; is a good bright line for players and Storytellers. Once that line is crossed, the resulting changes in setting flavor -- and possibly gameplay, depending on the interests of your players -- can shift the game into an undesired thematic space full of smallpox vaccines, weaponized anthrax, homebrewed C-4, and suitcase nukes. A lot of traditional pulp fantasy did run with the idea that magic was purely an add-on to Scientific Knowledge As We Now Know It, but not all, and the resulting flavor is not to everyone's taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T15:01:45-08:00","id":47630,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://media.lunch.com/d/d7/164442.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> &quot;Germs?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Uh-huh. In the eighteenth century, no such thing, nada, nothing. No one ever imagined such a thing. No sane person, anyway. Ah! Ah! Along comes this doctor, uh, uh, uh, Semmelweis, Semmelweis. Semmelweis comes along. He's trying to convince people, well, other doctors mainly, that's there's these teeny tiny invisible bad things called germs that get into your body and make you sick. Ah? He's trying to get doctors to wash their hands. What is this guy? Crazy? Teeny, tiny, invisible? What do you call it? Uh-uh, germs? Huh? What? Now, cut to the 20th century. Last week, as a matter of fact, before I got dragged into this hellhole. I go in to order a burger in this fast food joint, and the guy drops it on the floor. Jim, he picks it up, he wipes it off, he hands it to me like it's all OK. 'What about the germs?' I say. He says, 'I don't believe in germs. Germs is just a plot they made up so they can sell you disinfectants and soaps.' Now he's crazy, right? See? Ah! Ah! There's no right, there's no wrong, there's only popular opinion. You... you... you believe in germs, right?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T15:42:33-08:00","id":47655,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>I'd like to thank the people who elected to report an inflammatory post instead of responding to it.<br /> <br /> As a general reminder, insulting and generalizing people who like an aspect of the game you do not is a group attack as are derogatory terms for people with downs syndrome.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:11:13-08:00","id":47672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47542#post47542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ex2 disease descriptions, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, somebody really dropped the ball there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like thinking of things in terms of symbolism rather than practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meaning what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T17:31:51-08:00","id":47741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47601#post47601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Only stuff visible to the naked eye matches our modern knowledge base&quot; is a good bright line for players and Storytellers. Once that line is crossed, the resulting changes in setting flavor -- and possibly gameplay, depending on the interests of your players -- can shift the game into an undesired thematic space full of smallpox vaccines, weaponized anthrax, homebrewed C-4, and suitcase nukes. A lot of traditional pulp fantasy did run with the idea that magic was purely an add-on to Scientific Knowledge As We Now Know It, but not all, and the resulting flavor is not to everyone's taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always preferred &quot;Take as a given that the game runs on bacteria and viruses and cell division <i>et al</i> and then never mention it because it's not relevant&quot; to &quot;Try to be clever by working out the implications of the setting <i>not</i> running on bacteria and viruses and cell division <i>et al</i>.&quot; The latter sticks in my craw something fierce. It's <i>wank.</i> And I always hated the 2e disease descriptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T17:35:21-08:00","id":47748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47741#post47741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always preferred &quot;Take as a given that the game runs on bacteria and viruses and cell division <i>et al</i> and then never mention it because it's not relevant&quot; to &quot;Try to be clever by working out the implications of the setting <i>not</i> running on bacteria and viruses and cell division <i>et al</i>.&quot; The latter sticks in my craw something fierce. It's <i>wank.</i> And I always hated the 2e disease descriptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I learned anything from running games, it's that if something is true, players <i>will </i>make it relevant.<br /> <br /> Player inventivity is not always a good thing for a game's theme, mood or plot, unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T17:40:31-08:00","id":47749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47748#post47748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I learned anything from running games, it's that if something is true, players <i>will </i>make it relevant.<br /> <br /> Player inventivity is not always a good thing for a game's theme, mood or plot, unfortunately.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you talking about? Please, outline the problem to me. Because if you're going to say something like &quot;My players decide to invent antibiotics and vaccines,&quot; first of all that's not how invention works (antibiotics were discovered by accident), and second of all GMs have been shutting that stuff down effectively since D&amp;D players started using flour to clear out dungeons with fuel-air bombs and researching how trebuchets work IRL so they could describe their characters making them.<br /> <br /> If you don't want your players inventing modern medical science with high-success Medicine rolls, you can do it by not letting them invent modern medical science with high-success Medicine rolls just as easily as you can do it by declaring that in Creation, diseases run on magic bullshit, and the former is also less passive-aggressive.<br /> <br /> (Do not drop personal anecdotes on me like they're the fucking received wisdom of the ancients.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 01-12-2014, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T17:54:25-08:00","id":47759,"title":"","content":"This thread <i>started </i>with the idea of &quot;virusmen.&quot; Now, viruses don't work that way, but choleramen and plaguemen and whatever... Urgh. Of course I'd shut that down, but it's not a singular point, and it's not about inventing modern medical science either. It's about the fact that if the setting runs on cellular biology and bacteria, people will treat it as running on cellular biology and bacteria, and come up with solutions and applications pertaining to cellular biology and bacteria. The alternative is to say &quot;the world runs on cellular biology and bacteria, but you can't treat it as such,&quot; which is a lame answer. If it has no relevance to the game, it shouldn't be there, and the setting should work in a manner that correlates to the mood and themes it is supposed to carry. <br /> <br /> That is to say, if you shouldn't be inventing antibiotics, then make it so you can't invente antibiotics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T17:57:29-08:00","id":47761,"title":"","content":"The actual solution is to take as a given that the world runs on cellular biology and bacteria, and then not care, because the alternative is to invent some other way the world works, and whatever other way that is, it will be just as full of possible stupid-ass extrapolations counter to intended mood and theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T18:22:26-08:00","id":47773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47672#post47672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meaning what?</div> </div> </div> </div>In this instance, it means that I'd concieve of, say, tuberculosis as a nebulous <i>thing</i> which is both the cause of tuberculosis and the symptoms thereof, rather than the mycobacterial infection I know it to be.<br /> <br /> It's vaguely related to how, in <b>Mage</b>, transforming the pure carbon of a diamond into wood requires deeper understanding of Matter than doing the same to a piece of glass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T18:23:33-08:00","id":47774,"title":"","content":"Or it could be a fun supernatural setting with interesting in-theme implications to be delved into by the players and fitting its ancient world aesthetics, rather than filing it away as &quot;counter-thematic things never to be explored!&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, either/or.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T18:41:01-08:00","id":47786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47761#post47761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actual solution is to take as a given that the world runs on cellular biology and bacteria, and then not care, because the alternative is to invent some other way the world works, and whatever other way that is, it will be just as full of possible stupid-ass extrapolations counter to intended mood and theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I would never take a solution which require me to demand that my players don't care about the world of our game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/613-vegetalss4","name":"Vegetalss4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar613_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T19:21:52-08:00","id":47803,"title":"","content":"Virusmen.<br /> <br /> I am weeping openly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T19:27:24-08:00","id":47805,"title":"","content":"I bypass much of the problem by adopting a traditional-eastern-like take on it. Under such a paradigm, emulating Feng shui, 5-element theory, Yin-Yang theory and so on, there is little need to delve into the specifics of biology or chemistry as understood by modern science.<br /> <br /> Now, if you are unfamiliar with the concepts that surround traditional Chinese medicine (which also pertains to their ancient understanding of the way the universe / nature works) that would be a lot of material to study just to sporadically help maintain verisimilitude in a game. Luckily for me, I already study it as part of my work, so I just have to fudge the details to have it sound right for Exalted.<br /> <br /> If anyone here plays Weapons of the Gods or Legends of the Wulin, those games include enough info about such concepts that if you are good at winging the details and not worrying overmuch about small details and minor inconsistencies you could take a similar approach as mine. Or just read some articles on Wikipedia* XD<br /> <br /> *The one on the 5 elements manages to lay out the basics in a pretty concise manner. There are a few tidbits there that are different from the information I learned, though not all sources agree on them anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T19:29:47-08:00","id":47807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47803#post47803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Virusmen.<br /> <br /> I am weeping openly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Come on, Holden. Downward Fire, a barnacle-totem Lunar who leads a roving barbarian tribe of syphilis-men. Tell me that's not the sickest shit ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:00:52-08:00","id":47822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47774#post47774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or it could be a fun supernatural setting with interesting in-theme implications to be delved into by the players and fitting its ancient world aesthetics, rather than filing it away as &quot;counter-thematic things never to be explored!&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, either/or.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's tricky and perhaps something that should be decided table-to-table rather than established concretely in the manual (the way 2e did.)<br /> <br /> Part of the premise of any fantasy game is that it's set in a world where at least <i>some</i> of the magical thinking people do or have once applied to the world is true, but I don't think it's possible or valuable to over-analyze the dividing line between reality and fantasy (especially since, by definition, it's not going to make sense, because magical thinking just <i>doesn't</i> when you really look hard at it.)<br /> <br /> If a player thinks up a cool thing to do using a degree of basic germ-based medical knowledge that their character could plausibly deduce (like having their Twilight who has a lot of recovered First Age knowledge inexplicably insist on boiling all their medical tools even when everyone else thinks it's a bizarre quirk), that's cool and there's no reason to stop them. Conversely, if someone has a cool idea based on some magical interpretation of the world, I think it's fine to say &quot;sure, why not&quot; and go with that. Since those are the only times this is ever likely to come up, there's no point in nailing it down.<br /> <br /> Virusmen are still goofy, though. <a href=\"http://video.disney.com/watch/wizards-duel-4be36b86f6d55e5bc7f6b2d6\" target=\"_blank\">Disney Wizard duels</a> not withstanding.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Bah, that video doesn't show the end of the duel. Oh well. Merlin turns into a virus and wins. Technically he's cheating because they're not animals, and the rules specified only animals...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:28:28-08:00","id":47845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vegetalss4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47786#post47786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I would never take a solution which require me to demand that my players don't care about the world of our game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand the way in which I mean &quot;Don't care.&quot; Go read She Who Lives In Her Name's description in Games of Divinity, and pay attention to the bit where she broke three of her spheres against Creation and diminished it. That was an awesome bit of background fluff up until the very moment people started caring about it and calling it the Three Spheres Cataclysm and extrapolating from it, at which point it started ruining things. Does this mean it never should have been printed? No, because it's great in the context in which it initially appears. It means people shouldn't have started caring about it.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Creation runs on germ theory, and that's great. But it's not relevant. Making a bit deal out of it is going to cause problems. Swapping it out for something that's safe to make a big deal out of is going to cause even bigger problems, because whatever you replace it with is going to be some stupid-ass shit. And, I'm sorry not sorry to say, if you insist that everything in the setting should be something you can make a big deal out of, you're going to have a dumb cartoon setting in about five seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:34:38-08:00","id":47850,"title":"","content":"Either way, I think it's probably best if the books don't actually discuss germ theory and such either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:36:55-08:00","id":47853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47850#post47850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, I think it's probably best if the books don't actually discuss germ theory and such either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. It would be just as bad for the books to explicitly confirm it as explicitly deny it. However, when describing the setting, it is more useful for authors to look at actual behavior of actual diseases when describing how diseases work than to start thinking &quot;Diseases in Creation don't work according to germ theory, so I don't need to do research.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:41:16-08:00","id":47856,"title":"","content":"Incidentally you can very easily have plant-people and fungus-people via Wyld influence or the influence of strong elemental essence. I don't think it's appropriate for Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:41:26-08:00","id":47857,"title":"","content":"My take on the whole thing is that, if you perform medical care on someone based on the internal flows of essence through their body according to some derivation of Five Element Theory, that should work, because Creation runs on essence and stuff.<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't necessarily have to invalidate operating on someone via the germ theory of disease or cellular mechanics or whatever. Just, most people in Creation would be much more likely to go after five element theory first, since that's probably the general wisdom and, even if you've studied First Age Medical Manuals, they're probably going to teach all of it, since the five element theory was probably devised first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:43:03-08:00","id":47859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47822#post47822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Bah, that video doesn't show the end of the duel. Oh well. Merlin turns into a virus and wins. Technically he's cheating because they're not animals, and the rules specified only animals...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mim's rules also specified &quot;no make-believe things like pink dragons and such.&quot; I suppose it's possible the world is oddly specific enough that pink dragons are a go-to example of &quot;make-believe things,&quot; while purple dragons are not, but... Yeah, that's about the only way she didn't cheat, and far more blatantly at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:47:06-08:00","id":47861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47807#post47807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the sickest</div> </div> </div> </div>pfffffffft","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\" target=\"_blank\">To the extent possible under law, I hereby waive all copyright and related or neighboring rights to this post.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/666-eco-mono","name":"Eco-Mono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar666_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:47:52-08:00","id":47865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47857#post47857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on the whole thing is that, if you perform medical care on someone based on the internal flows of essence through their body according to some derivation of Five Element Theory, that should work, because Creation runs on essence and stuff.<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't necessarily have to invalidate operating on someone via the germ theory of disease or cellular mechanics or whatever. Just, most people in Creation would be much more likely to go after five element theory first, since that's probably the general wisdom and, even if you've studied First Age Medical Manuals, they're probably going to teach all of it, since the five element theory was probably devised first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, conventional medicine in Creation is often going to be about essence flows and things, like, it's going to discuss real medical phenomena <i>in the context of</i> some sort of elemental essence flow theory, and it's going to be highly developed in a way that both works and harmonizes well with medical magic, which actually <i>does</i> run on essence flows. Maybe they'll talk about how cleanliness is important because its opposite creates disorder and invites malign influences, which is, uh, literally true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:58:20-08:00","id":47870,"title":"","content":"Edit: Deleted, because I don't think I <i>can</i> approach this topic in a way that's not an attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":615,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","user":"The Hanged Man","date":". 01-13-2014, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T21:00:10-08:00","id":47873,"title":"","content":"(Part of my bias against magic bullshit diseases is that I'm pretty sure we're not capable of coming up with off-the-cuff magic bullshit diseases that behave in fashions <i>more interesting</i> than actual real diseases do in real life. &quot;Cholera happens when you let criminals bathe in your water&quot; works way better as something people believe about cholera, which is wrong, than it works as an actual in-setting cholera fact.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T21:05:25-08:00","id":47877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47803#post47803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Virusmen.<br /> <br /> I am weeping openly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go to a doctor, maybe?<br /> <br /> Woowoowoowoowoo (Scuttles away)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T21:45:31-08:00","id":47911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47803#post47803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Virusmen.<br /> <br /> I am weeping openly.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then you couldn't have these guys!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6o0DfD6D3oM\" data-code=\"6o0DfD6D3oM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/6o0DfD6D3oM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T01:42:12-08:00","id":48013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47845#post47845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, I'm sorry not sorry to say, if you insist that everything in the setting should be something you can make a big deal out of, you're going to have a dumb cartoon setting in about five seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting position. I've taken soul theory to the n'th degree in my Autochthon game and it only comes off as gritty and a bit scary. I've got some plantmen several arcs in the future and they are neither cartoony nor silly. I think you can spin most anything to be most anything. The Fay is an example of that - I've no doubt they were meant to be taken seriously as presented but they are pretty much a joke to most of the community. There is confidence that need not be the case and they are still in the setting.<br /> <br /> Many things can be taken extremely far, every great scientist has done that, it must simply fall to equally great occult scholars and scientists in Exalted. If anything - when the lore/occult monkeys are spouting stuff off that makes a normal persons head spin? Your doing it right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T01:55:34-08:00","id":48014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47856#post47856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally you can very easily have plant-people and fungus-people via Wyld influence or the influence of strong elemental essence. I don't think it's appropriate for Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Treebeard for 2014 Lunar Elder","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T03:42:18-08:00","id":48050,"title":"","content":"Well, better late than never.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, this reminds me of a discussion pertaining to postmodern analysis of the matter of disease killing a Ramses.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This statement of Latour's is really on par with Baudrillard's quip that the Gulf War never happened in that it's not meant to describe what happened to physical bodies, but the way they are captured by language. Latour is saying that a scientific understanding of what killed Ramses is constructed one way, but this is not the social reality of how he died, which was constructed another way. According to Latour's thought, neither is a simple description of reality, but a social construction based on interpreting observations. This doesn't mean the bacillus isn't real.<br /> <br /> If we were to take this to a thought experiment and travel in time to show an ancient Egyptian the microrganisms that killed his king, he might construct a different story with the same data. For example, he might not divide the organisms and the mechanism of its infection into separate entities. This holistic description would be very strange to us, and it's hard for us to get into that guy's sandals. Taken further, if the time-displaced Egyptian used these categories of thought as the basis for scientific inquiries with the help of all of our modern toys and data, he might discover things that we can't, because of the way in which we build scientific facts. In no case do the physical phenomena actually cease the exist or even change. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T04:33:29-08:00","id":48066,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/4pBCzd6.png\" target=\"_blank\">Dryads</a> have babies too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T05:54:09-08:00","id":48105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48050#post48050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, better late than never.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, this reminds me of a discussion pertaining to postmodern analysis of the matter of disease killing a Ramses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's about as relevant a quote as you can apply to this discussion. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T06:56:49-08:00","id":48131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=47865#post47865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, yeah, conventional medicine in Creation is often going to be about essence flows and things, like, it's going to discuss real medical phenomena <i>in the context of</i> some sort of elemental essence flow theory, and it's going to be highly developed in a way that both works and harmonizes well with medical magic, which actually <i>does</i> run on essence flows. Maybe they'll talk about how cleanliness is important because its opposite creates disorder and invites malign influences, which is, uh, literally true.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a note, while most of 2e gets railed on for stupid shit, <i>Scroll of Kings</i> did have its moments of just using real world logic well. When it talked about jungle warfare in the East, it mostly said the reasons that jungle warfare sucked: you die from horrible infectious diseases due to filthy water and perfect breeding conditions for this. One could argue it's because of Wood Essence inbalance in the region. And that's kind of right. That Wood Essence overcharge of the Direction means more life. More life means more parasites and horrible infectious agents to be extra fecund and eat you, causing infections and making you horribly sick.<br /> <br /> Real world germ theory can be incorperated into Creation without too much weirdness. About the only thing I wonder on at time are viruses, but that's because I'm pretty damned sure if over talking of biological workings of Creation is one thing that doesn't matter, molecular and atomic theory is even moreso something that day to day doesn't fucking matter.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T07:03:08-08:00","id":48136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48066#post48066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/4pBCzd6.png\" target=\"_blank\">Dryads</a> have babies too!</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\">And the baby sometimes has a Beastman for their adoptive father</span>, while their real father is a...Dawn? Dusk? Battles? Some sort of warlike Exalt","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T07:36:39-08:00","id":48156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48136#post48136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">And the baby sometimes has a Beastman for their adoptive father</span>, while their real father is a...Dawn? Dusk? Battles? Some sort of warlike Exalt</div> </div> </div> </div>And the child's first words are &quot;FUCKING SHIT&quot;, gleefuly shouted to the four winds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T07:46:54-08:00","id":48162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48136#post48136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">And the baby sometimes has a Beastman for their adoptive father</span>, while their real father is a...Dawn? Dusk? Battles? Some sort of warlike Exalt</div> </div> </div> </div>Pity the Beastman couldn't have been the biological father in this case; I mean, c'mon, topiary animal person babies!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T08:25:32-08:00","id":48186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48162#post48162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pity the Beastman couldn't have been the biological father in this case; I mean, c'mon, topiary animal person babies!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it'd certainly bring a new meaning to &quot;timberwolf&quot;....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T08:42:26-08:00","id":48196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48014#post48014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Treebeard for 2014 Lunar Elder</div> </div> </div> </div>We have Exigents and old, spiritually-developed Wood Aspects for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T08:56:04-08:00","id":48209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48196#post48196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We have Exigents and old, spiritually-developed Wood Aspects for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this means we can't also have Lunars for that, why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:05:23-08:00","id":48214,"title":"","content":"Because Lunars aren't tree people.<br /> <br /> Now, a Lunar who invokes the imagery of the more ambiguous book Ents, where it's possible they're adorned with some kind of tree clothing, that I can get behind. Especially if it comes across like sloths who are so sessile that they start being covered in algae (not that I don't mean that the Lunars is transformed when this happens).<br /> <br /> Lunars can transform into all kinds of things, but I think they'd be diminished if one lent their core assumptions the aesthetics of everything they can transform into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:51:28-08:00","id":48258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48214#post48214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Lunars aren't tree people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because... ?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunars can transform into all kinds of things, but I think they'd be diminished if one lent their core assumptions the aesthetics of everything they can transform into. </div> </div> </div>.. Okay? I don't. Lunars are best to me when they're shifting into weird creatures, and plant-men fits the bill. I mean it ain't like they're the Plant People Exalted, but I see no reason it shouldn't be a thing they can do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:57:12-08:00","id":48266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48214#post48214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Lunars aren't tree people.<br /> <br /> Now, a Lunar who invokes the imagery of the more ambiguous book Ents, where it's possible they're adorned with some kind of tree clothing, that I can get behind. Especially if it comes across like sloths who are so sessile that they start being covered in algae (not that I don't mean that the Lunars is transformed when this happens).<br /> <br /> Lunars can transform into all kinds of things, but I think they'd be diminished if one lent their core assumptions the aesthetics of everything they can transform into.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree, Jutlander isn't asking to make virus/tree-lunars canon and in-theme, he's just asking if and how it can be done. And it can. In fact, with 2.5e you can pour enough bp into essence to start with a tree totem and the Laurels and Ivy knack (iirc it's essence 4. You'd need a couple flaws at chargen.). Everything he wants to do is possible under the 2.5 rules, whether or not it <i>should</i> be possible.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm not a big fan of plant-Lunars because it goes directly against their hunters/predators theme and imo makes them a little too close for comfort to DnD Druids... but meh, if he wants advice on how to do it, with rules that specifically allow him to do it, might as well help out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T10:00:38-08:00","id":48273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48258#post48258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because... ?<br /> .. Okay? I don't. Lunars are best to me when they're shifting into weird creatures, and plant-men fits the bill. I mean it ain't like they're the Plant People Exalted, but I see no reason it shouldn't be a thing they can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars aren't supposed to be every shapeshifter or weird-looking thing out in the wilderness. Where;s the room for the Numina of the Mist? The Exalted of Forest Gods? Things from that Wyld that thankfully don't all fall under the envelope of Fair Folk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T10:06:22-08:00","id":48278,"title":"","content":"I suppose there isn't actually any rule against taking a concubine into the Wyld and then using Laurel and Hardy Method to take the form of the tree from Evil Dead. Presumably events proceed naturally from there, although I would rather not picture the problems with splinters.<br /> <br /> If you prefer men, take the form of a tree with a knothole in it.<br /> <br /> Really this doesn't bear thinking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T10:15:26-08:00","id":48284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48266#post48266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree, Jutlander isn't asking to make virus/tree-lunars canon and in-theme</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not, but Imrix seems a bit contentious against denial of even a facetious idea that a canon Lunar should resemble one of his Argent Witches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T10:26:47-08:00","id":48294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48273#post48273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars aren't supposed to be every shapeshifter or weird-looking thing out in the wilderness. Where;s the room for the Numina of the Mist? The Exalted of Forest Gods? Things from that Wyld that thankfully don't all fall under the envelope of Fair Folk?</div> </div> </div> </div>The room, as you put it, is in the realization that aesthetic overlap happens, and it's not a terrible thing. Especially with a splat for whom one of the big shticks is stealing other peoples shapes. If anything, the fact that these things exist, and that Lunars are supposed to be infiltrators and shapeshifting spies, rather leans toward the idea that Lunars should be able to assume the forms of, and/or similar to, Forest Witches or Numina.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48284#post48284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe not, but Imrix seems a bit contentious against denial of even a facetious idea that a canon Lunar should resemble one of his Argent Witches.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, what do Argent Witches have to do with this? Where did I give the impression I was talking about them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 01-13-2014, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T10:37:54-08:00","id":48303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48294#post48294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The room, as you put it, is in the realization that aesthetic overlap happens, and it's not a terrible thing. Especially with a splat for whom one of the big shticks is stealing other peoples shapes. If anything, the fact that these things exist, and that Lunars are supposed to be infiltrators and shapeshifting spies, rather leans toward the idea that Lunars should be able to assume forms similar to Forest Witches or Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you could just sneak in using a shape common to the forest. It's not like it's bereft of wildlife, or that you'll be easily noticed. Of course, it could also be that the whole &quot;spy and infiltrator!&quot; thing is a tad overplayed, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T10:40:41-08:00","id":48305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48294#post48294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, what do Argent Witches have to do with this? Where did I give the impression I was talking about them?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunars are best to me when they're shifting into weird creatures, and plant-men fits the bill. </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's more like Argent Witches and your opinion on plantmen are both effects of your preferred aesthetics for Lunars, rather than your opinion on plantmen coming from Argent Witches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T10:45:14-08:00","id":48307,"title":"","content":"You could, yeah. I don't see why Lunars should be limited to that. If Lunars can acquire the shapes of beasts and humanoids, why should they be barred from Spirits or stranger things? Lunars must be able to acquire at least the forms of Primordial Deva's, so it can't be a question of power, and are you really going to try and say that the soul heirarchy of the Titans is somehow less strange to mortal minds than the Behemoths they filled Creation with?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48305#post48305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it's more like Argent Witches and your opinion on plantmen are both effects of your preferred aesthetics for Lunars, rather than your opinion on plantmen coming from Argent Witches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably! Then again, these aesthetics were hardly foreign to Lunars even prior to the Witches - Shifting Penumbra Stance is pretty cool, yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 01-13-2014, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T10:48:31-08:00","id":48312,"title":"","content":"Lunars shapechanging into trees and gods is sort of like Solars slipping outside of fate with high-Essence Stealth Charms -- it's a thing they can do, but it's not really something they're naturally attuned to. Just because you can learn a Charm to turn into a tree doesn't mean turning into a tree then expands everything your fundamental magical abilities can do.<br /> <br /> (Lunars probably shouldn't be able to make demon-blooded people by doing the beastman-with-two-backs while wearing demon form, either.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T10:56:42-08:00","id":48316,"title":"","content":"I suppose this may seem a lot more sensible when I can see the material for 3e Lunars, whenever that is. Right now though it just comes off like baseless, nonsensical assertions to me. For my part, a Lunar seeding Malfeas with his own demonblooded offspring, creating a network of spies and loyal servants for his own reasons, seems like a pretty cool setup.<br /> <br /> Nothing to do but wait I guess!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 01-13-2014, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T11:51:27-08:00","id":48362,"title":"","content":"How about... banana-men, very randy ones<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://features.cgsociety.org/newgallerycrits/g06/29806/29806_1236311607_large.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T11:57:15-08:00","id":48369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=45848#post45848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it might be kind of distressing -- esp. the actual moment of Exaltation -- I dunno if this would quite work as sabotage. Terrestrials are immune to the hazards of their animas, as I recall. They might wind up seeming even more deified. Burning bush men!<br /> <br /> EDIT: If viewed as holy, they <i>would</i> probably -- reverently but firmly -- be made to live apart from the rest of society, granted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but given that anima flaring is very common during Exaltations, what happens when every teenager is potentially a bomb waiting to explode - er, Exalt - especially in dramatic situations (which, teenagers being teenagers, they might naturally seek to create)?<br /> <br /> And are Fire Aspects immune to other Fire Aspects' animas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/240-winged-cat","name":"Winged Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar240_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T12:25:35-08:00","id":48393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Winged Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48369#post48369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, but given that anima flaring is very common during Exaltations, what happens when every teenager is potentially a bomb waiting to explode - er, Exalt - especially in dramatic situations (which, teenagers being teenagers, they might naturally seek to create)?<br /> <br /> <b>And are Fire Aspects immune to other Fire Aspects' animas?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you know how the Terrestrials keep starting fires?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T12:36:15-08:00","id":48403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48393#post48393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't you know how the Terrestrials keep starting fires?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's their desire!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T12:47:54-08:00","id":48411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48403#post48403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's their desire!</div> </div> </div> </div>Danger danger!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T13:21:17-08:00","id":48431,"title":"","content":"A few things:<br /> <br /> 1) The totem will always be an animal. It specifically says so in the manual.<br /> <br /> 2) The Lunar does not have to be in any shape but human. The Charm listed in the original post allows human Lunars to sex up human humans and apply features from any of their known shapes.<br /> <br /> 3) To have this Charm plus the Knack that allows for them to assume non-animal shapes is very specialized. To actually combine the two to make fungusmen is something that would be a once-in-Age thing and not &quot;the new silver&quot;. I find it comparable to the Cthulhu Solar of the First Age. Possible, but freakishly rare. And freakish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":864,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","user":"Jutlander","date":". 01-13-2014, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T14:05:25-08:00","id":48459,"title":"","content":"I'm very conflicted about whether there should be plant-aspected Lunars*. On one hand, I think it'd be very interesting: Treebeard, Poison Ivy, Swamp-Thing are all pretty great characters. On the other, how do you fit them into Lunars without it feeling like &quot;oh yeah, and there are some plant-Lunars too, but we aren't really going to put much effort into them&quot; because Lunar charms are going to channel animals de facto (if not de jure).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Lunars have problems. While the devs have sold me on the fact that they can fix their fluff (see: Holden's spiel on barbarians, among other gems from the old forums), I haven't seen much about fixing the mechanical aspects (including but not limited to the Silver Solars bit that everyone is tired of talking about and which I do not wish to re-open).<br /> <br /> In my mind, expanding Lunars to include plants could theoretically add flavor/definition to the Lunars, but it could also weaken their schtick significantly as well. It'd be a really tough thing to accomplish. The Lunar identity is already weak: the deliberate downplaying of body horror is understandable but also very limiting. I was playing around with this in my head a few days ago... the closest I came to anything half-decent was Lunars being in complete control of their own body. This includes everything from myosin-strengthened bound to steady heart-rate insinuation to feline-tapetum stare. Lots of permanent charms that improve the body, with 'burst' charms that could produce a related effect coming off of those permanents. Giving them very relaxed dice-limits would be interesting too. Solars get Attribute+Ability as max, Lunars get Attribute*2+Essence? Anything to make them more interesting...<br /> <br /> * Don't read into me saying 'aspect.' It was the first word that came into my head and has nothing to do with the caste vs. aspect debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/259-overshee","name":"Overshee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar259_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T14:31:47-08:00","id":48479,"title":"","content":"I recall that, per their &quot;barbarian&quot; aesthetic, Lunars evoke tribal culture heroes. Archetypes like Warrior, Trickster, and Shaman, and individuals like Cuchulainn. Such characters sometimes have strong associations to plants or other natural features (e.g. mountains, the sea) that seem like good sources of inspiration for characters where no specific animal feels relevant.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think it would be cool to see how a Lunar sailor in such a paradigm diverged from a Solar one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 01-13-2014, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T16:52:00-08:00","id":48583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48312#post48312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars shapechanging into trees and gods is sort of like Solars slipping outside of fate with high-Essence Stealth Charms -- it's a thing they can do, but it's not really something they're naturally attuned to. Just because you can learn a Charm to turn into a tree doesn't mean turning into a tree then expands everything your fundamental magical abilities can do.<br /> <br /> (Lunars probably shouldn't be able to make demon-blooded people by doing the beastman-with-two-backs while wearing demon form, either.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really feeling this argument in the context of the OP's question. I think there's a case for writing things differently in 3e, but in the context of 2e it really feels like a pull-the-rug-out ruling -- you've got a power that lets you add plant shapes to your Heart's Blood library and a power that lets you &quot;imprint the child with features from any shape in [your] Heart\u2019s Blood library, including [your] spirit shape, rather than being restricted to the form [you] currently [wear]&quot;, and while it's a little weird, it doesn't seem <i>so</i> weird that it justifies an exceptional ruling. so long as you stick to the basic rule that your kids are humans with some thematic mutations. The game made a point of <i>not</i> drawing a line between animal shapes and shapes you learn to take via specialized Knacks, after all. I see the demon-blooded case as a bit different insofar as demon-blooded are a specific thing -- siring children who have some traits that reflect the demon form yes, demon-blooded no.<br /> <br /> (On the whole I always felt the whole &quot;genetic engineering through fucking&quot; gimmick was overplayed as a Lunar theme. I think sexuality and weird sex have a place in the splat, but it sort of felt like it got emphasized to the extent it did because nobody was quite sure what to do with Lunars.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 01-13-2014, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T17:19:35-08:00","id":48604,"title":"","content":"I think that if you want to play a Lunar who spends a long time studying oaks, who then produces children with leaves and flowers in their hair or rough barklike skin, nobody is going to look at you strangely.<br /> <br /> That's just not a &quot;typical&quot; example of how Lunars work -- it's a strange edge-case that they can twist into by combining several powers, as evidenced by the fact that you needed two fairly obscure and situational knacks to even approach it. (You can produce beastmen right out of the box, but to produce children with even subtle plant features, you need both Laurel-and-Ivy Technique and then, since you can't reproduce with humans in plant form, you need another knack to let you imprint features and mutations without having to take plant form.)<br /> <br /> So it's not like it's not allowed, but you're never going to see Lunars doing it in the backstory, or canon charms specifically devoted to it or anything -- given that both the knacks are on the obscure and situational side, and there's no actual reason to <i>want</i> to do it in general, I wouldn't be surprised if there's maybe one or two Lunars who have produced meaningful numbers of kids with plantlike mutations, ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T18:39:13-08:00","id":48633,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think that's a good way to put it. It's probably not a good thing to put in the books, but if a player really wanted to do it and was prepared to have their character put the investment in and get the weird looks from their peers I'd be like &quot;yeah okay&quot; and wouldn't feel like I was leaning on Rule Zero.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I was reading about marginal life and pseudo-life and apparently there's a thing called <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultramicrobacteria\" target=\"_blank\">ultramicrobacteria</a>. So the real question is, can I play an ultramicrobacteriaman?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T19:19:16-08:00","id":48659,"title":"","content":"You're not going far enough - Prionmen for Ex3! <br /> <br /> &quot;All right, ST, what do I roll to stick my doodle in the transmissible spongiform encephalopathy?&quot;<br /> &quot;Kill me now.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T21:15:07-08:00","id":48708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48278#post48278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose there isn't actually any rule against taking a concubine into the Wyld and then using Laurel and Hardy Method to take the form of the tree from Evil Dead. Presumably events proceed naturally from there, although I would rather not picture the problems with splinters.<br /> <br /> If you prefer men, take the form of a tree with a knothole in it.<br /> <br /> <b>Really this doesn't bear thinking about</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And...what, 'conventional' beastman-spawning does? I mean, I agree that plantmen and fungusmen and virusmen <sub>(how would that even work? Would it be like one of those STM images of a stick-figure made of atoms, blown up to human scale with gangly limbs and a smiley face made out of giant bundles of prions?)</sub> don't really fit with core Lunar themes, but 1) core Lunar themes are a mess, and it's not like they aren't being rewritten for a new edition or anything, and 2) as long as you're going to mechanically-incentivize boning outside your shapeshifting character's species, Kingdom Animalia seems like a fairly arbitrary place to draw the line. Really, I'd prefer that beastmen and only beastmen remain for 3e, except this time with an explanation that isn't &quot;Somebody literally fucked a cat&quot;, but apparently that's not happening!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48312#post48312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars shapechanging into trees and gods is sort of like Solars slipping outside of fate with high-Essence Stealth Charms -- it's a thing they can do, but it's not really something they're naturally attuned to. Just because you can learn a Charm to turn into a tree doesn't mean turning into a tree then expands everything your fundamental magical abilities can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about mythic, god- or titan-spawned monstrosities a la Typhon and Echidna and their brood, or great divine beasts like the dragon/bird/tiger/turtle quartet who keep making their way into various works of Japanese pop-culture? It always annoyed me that you had to be fucking Int6Ess6 to get more out of beating a Celestial Lion than the satisfaction of punching its smug fucking face in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T16:20:22-08:00","id":49336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overshee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48459#post48459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very conflicted about whether there should be plant-aspected Lunars*. On one hand, I think it'd be very interesting: Treebeard, Poison Ivy, Swamp-Thing are all pretty great characters. On the other, how do you fit them into Lunars without it feeling like &quot;oh yeah, and there are some plant-Lunars too, but we aren't really going to put much effort into them&quot; because Lunar charms are going to channel animals de facto (if not de jure).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that Swamp Thing is already an Exalt. The Avatar of the Green could probably be ported almost directly into Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-14-2014, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T18:19:12-08:00","id":49416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=49336#post49336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that Swamp Thing is already an Exalt. The Avatar of the Green could probably be ported almost directly into Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>What sort of Exalt? Exigent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/259-overshee","name":"Overshee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar259_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T21:07:27-08:00","id":49533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overshee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=49416#post49416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What sort of Exalt? Exigent?</div> </div> </div> </div>More like an Infernal with an unhealthy fetish toward Metagaos charms. Metagaos is less Green and more Gray though, but that can be fix with a shit load of Green Sun Nimbus Flare upgrade charms !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 01-15-2014, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T00:11:44-08:00","id":49600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48431#post48431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few things:<br /> <br /> 1) The totem will always be an animal. It specifically says so in the manual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That's nice. It also says all Infernals have to diddle a transmorgrified 17 year old &quot;little girl&quot;, but you don't see many people around here following that.<br /> <br /> Somebody wants to play a person with a Weeping Willow or a Eucalyptus deglupta (google it, be amazed!) totem, I wouldn't stand in the way of that or support writing up the manual to stand in the way of that. Make like Man-Thing kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 01-15-2014, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T00:56:33-08:00","id":49613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overshee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=49416#post49416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What sort of Exalt? Exigent?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's really not a bad fit for the whole concept.<br /> In the current DC continuity Swamp Thing is basically the Chosen of the Green (Earth's plantlife) more specifically The Parliament of Trees which are something between his patrons and his past lives since when a Swamp Thing dies they take root and become part of the Parliament which allows their memories to be accessed.<br /> <br /> Being the defender of plantlife is more badass than it sounds because other forces of nature have their own avatars some of whom desire supremacy over all other forms of life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T02:12:42-08:00","id":49636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=49600#post49600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. That's nice. It also says all Infernals have to diddle a transmorgrified 17 year old &quot;little girl&quot;, but you don't see many people around here following that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Lunars being confined to animals as their spirit shape as a matter of thematic purity and coherance really as crass and objectionable as this?<br /> <br /> I mean, by this logic, nothing written in any of the books ever should be taken as something to actually use, because of this occasion where a book presented something that nobody wanted to use. Where's the line drawn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T02:18:25-08:00","id":49639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=48316#post48316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my part, a Lunar seeding Malfeas with his own demonblooded offspring, creating a network of spies and loyal servants for his own reasons, seems like a pretty cool setup.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you told me of a setup involving an Exalt seeding the demon realm with demon-blooded offspring, I'd assume that it was facilitated by the human Exalt having sex with demons.<br /> <br /> So it's all right, even if it has nothing to do with shapeshifting into a demon.<br /> <br /> A Lunar seeding the Realm with demon-blooded offspring is one that would actually suggest that the Lunar's shapeshifting was relevant, and would be where it would start to feel dissonant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T02:53:58-08:00","id":49658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=49613#post49613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's really not a bad fit for the whole concept.<br /> In the current DC continuity Swamp Thing is basically the Chosen of the Green (Earth's plantlife) more specifically The Parliament of Trees which are something between his patrons and his past lives since when a Swamp Thing dies they take root and become part of the Parliament which allows their memories to be accessed.<br /> <br /> Being the defender of plantlife is more badass than it sounds because other forces of nature have their own avatars some of whom desire supremacy over all other forms of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>But on the other hand, his automatic resurrection as long as plantlife exists makes him come across as more of a spirit than an Exalt to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T03:00:14-08:00","id":49661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=49639#post49639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you told me of a setup involving an Exalt seeding the demon realm with demon-blooded offspring, I'd assume that it was facilitated by the human Exalt having sex with demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Lunar seeding the Realm with demon-blooded offspring is one that would actually suggest that the Lunar's shapeshifting was relevant, and would be where it would start to feel dissonant. </div> </div> </div>Actually, that seems, if anything, an even cooler setup to me. Lunars are at war with the realm after all, and that kind of covert messing with geneology seems the perfect way to degrade the Realm on the sly. Okay they get some demon-bloods out of the deal, which is better than unExalted mortals, but it's still not a DB.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 01-15-2014, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T03:46:07-08:00","id":49673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=49600#post49600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. That's nice. It also says all Infernals have to diddle a transmorgrified 17 year old &quot;little girl&quot;, but you don't see many people around here following that.<br /> <br /> Somebody wants to play a person with a Weeping Willow or a Eucalyptus deglupta (google it, be amazed!) totem, I wouldn't stand in the way of that or support writing up the manual to stand in the way of that. Make like Man-Thing kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just trying to clarify what the intent of my original post was (i.e. discuss whether this combination of Knack and Charm allows Lunars to create non-conventional x-men* under the official rules).<br /> <br /> I realize that I can ignore anything in any book, but it hardly furthers a meaningful conversation about the limits of rules and themes to simply say &quot;Ignore everything ever because child abuse&quot;.<br /> <br /> * Go on. Make the mutation joke. You know you want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T04:35:20-08:00","id":49689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamantineRapier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=49658#post49658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on the other hand, his automatic resurrection as long as plantlife exists makes him come across as more of a spirit than an Exalt to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Story-wise his ability to reconstitute himself has more in common with a Wounds Mean Nothing style perfect soak than how spirits regenerate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T09:03:19-08:00","id":49848,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the food for thought, Lioness.<br /> <br /> Still not sure where I fall on the 'should plant-lunars be a thing' debate, but my gut is telling me adding it as an option in the book would be more trouble than it's worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/259-overshee","name":"Overshee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar259_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T10:05:50-08:00","id":49875,"title":"","content":"I'm perfectly fine with Plant/Fungi folk. But the Virus/Single Celled folk is a more challenging question. I guess the question would be what traits do you want these humans to have, because they would be human after all. It would I guess involve simulating the simple organism trick with a large organism, so things like simple or redundant organs, similar to organelles. Malleable form? Similarity between members? Replicating the simple machine like physiology of viruses? What?<br /> <br /> And this of course is a threshold to greater questions. It leads one to believe that once this becomes possible Lunars could also develop tricks to make &quot;Beastmen&quot; from their Rock, Mountain, and Lake Forms. Or some combination like making Beastmen from multiple forms, or tacking your God Form with your Rhino Form and your Mountain form to make Halfcast/Beastmen/Rhino Godblooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T13:44:53-08:00","id":50038,"title":"","content":"For all we know, the original DBs might have come from the union of Luna or some Lunars with primal aspects of Creation (at Gaia's direction; perhaps Gaia wove this aspect into Luna after falling for her), and such acts by modern Lunars would create more.<br /> <br /> This would resolve the whole issue: &quot;beastmen&quot; of things close enough to a certain element type come out as DBs of that type. Plantmen are Wood DBs, rockmen are Earth DBs, and so on. Between birth and Exaltation, they show traits that any young Legendary Breeding DB-to-be would show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/240-winged-cat","name":"Winged Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar240_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T01:55:05-08:00","id":50529,"title":"","content":"I always figured the medical treatment worked because, in the clearly-magic setting of Exalted, that IS how diseases are created, and dealt with. If someone gets infected with consumption, it's because they were dominated and abused by those more powerful than them, which for some incomprehensible-to-humans (particularly us-humans, who are more-or-less used to a physical explanation for stuff) reason is kind of like an accidental spell that sets off this reaction in the victim. He responds to ginseng etc not because of an antibiotic effect, but because, for the same reason, that is anathema (if you'll pardon the term) to the workings of the &quot;spell&quot;. Cholera is <i>created</i> by criminals bathing in open water, because of their impurity or lack of justice, which causes the essence to warp in such a way to literally harm the god of the body of water, who spreads it on because, well, it's a god of water. Purification rituals don't affect little bacteria in the water, they affect the god, cleansing it of the impurity created by the criminal/goat, which means no more spreading of the disease.<br /> <br /> It's <i>Exalted</i>. Trying to tie it to real-world explanations kind of misses the whole point. When I watch fantasy movies, I don't bitch about how the magic violates the conservation of energy, or why the lightening bolt doesn't instantly earth itself after being cast: the wizard throws the lightening bolt with magic. Magic != science.<br /> <br /> Our world works, in broad, because physics. Exalted works, in broad, because gods and magic.<br /> <br /> But back to the main point. Could you create virusmen/bacteriamen if you combo the right Knacks? Sure. It'd require those entities to exist, but hey, it's your game, and if it makes it more fun than more power to you. Course, it requires like 3 or 4 Knacks, to get the right <i>kind</i> of virus or bacteria for the kind of people you want to make, and frankly has finite use in my eyes (although, given mortal susceptibility to disease, trying to address that angle does seem in line with the Silver Paths goals), but given that it explicitly states that Lunars were given the gift of change and flexibility, changing the assumptions that they only can turn into animals like wolves or squirrels seems right in the theme. Plus, nobody would see a normal, if sickly, looking individual moving in and, just by going about their daily normal lives, spreading disease, possibly productively, coming. And who is better at hiding their agenda and methods than the Lunar? (Apart from the Sid, mayhap).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 01-16-2014, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T03:51:48-08:00","id":50571,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm a little sad that I have to point this out, but, uh...well. One of the things I tell my prospective Exalted players to suck 'em into the game is that Exalted is a kitchen-sink setting. I generally challenge them to think of something they'd like in a game, then briefly describe the part of Exalted's vast setting that is that thing. So.<br /> <br /> Theoretical Prospective Player: Hey, Guru? I've been looking at Lunars, they're like humans with a totem animal that gives them powers, right? Can I play a guy who's like, a virusman? Like a living disease given physical form, or a guy with virus-like traits?<br /> <br /> Me: ...actually, yeah. See, way back in the ancient dawn of time there was a mighty civilization of sorcerer-priests who worshiped and studied the life energy in all things, known to other cultures as the Genesis Lords. Their magic was all about reshaping and repurposing life: living ships, geckos that live on your ceiling and luminesce when you clap, magically altered diseases that they'd inject into you to fight off other diseases...theirs was a small but mighty empire, and so the Chosen of the Sun grew jealous of their power and waged war upon them. Most of them died, and many fled on a great living ship into the madness beyond the world...but a few elite warrior-priests rendered their consciousness down into viral forms to wait out the destruction. Every now and then someone in Creation will come down with a case of the sniffles, and her personality will slowly begin to change as she dreams of an ancient city with spires of green filled with iridescent birds. Over time, she forgets who she is as the long-dead Genesis Lord takes over, gradually remembering more and more of himself and his ancient lore. They are subtle, these Genesis Lords, and many of them work to build a world where Creation will once again be safe for their kind, who they hope to revive from a few drops of blood or a drop of sweat or a fingerprint. They burn out the bodies they wear quickly, and when they die they wake again in someone else somewhere in Creation with a nasty stomach flu, and must again wait for their memories to slowly return.<br /> <br /> ...I guess I could let you play one of them. You'd definitely have some control over diseases and some knowledge of the physical and mystic building blocks of life.<br /> <br /> Theoretical Prospective Player: ...wait. You mean I can play a Time Lord?<br /> <br /> Me: Well, I did say Exalted has everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T04:57:01-08:00","id":50585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=50529#post50529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's <i>Exalted</i>. Trying to tie it to real-world explanations kind of misses the whole point.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the game with all the in-depth anthropology and sociology and economics?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T06:15:10-08:00","id":50609,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to go back and reiterate that when you get all excessively wanky about how disease works, you probably wind up with something that doesn't function the least bit like disease in real life, and that both removes a lot of the resonance, and a lot of the actual relevant implications of disease in play.<br /> <br /> I mean, when cholera is called the besieging army's bane in First Edition, that's kind of an implication that if you have your army of tens of thousands of people squat down in the same place for months on end, their local water supply is going to get mixed up with their toilets, and that's going to leave them ravaged by disease.<br /> <br /> So your biggest problem with portraying cholera as a thing that happens when criminals bathe in water is that, well... you're probably going to have an army that isn't ravaged by disease, and that's kind of a big deal for every army ever.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason that disease is so resonant and terrifying is because it spreads in a manner that, when you have the perspective on it that we do, we would expect of highly transmittable microscopic organisms. Indeed, part of the reason that people attach disease to easily parsed social narratives, often predicated on scapegoating, is because of just how terrifying disease is for the fact that nobody can really figure out how it's happening.<br /> <br /> And capturing that is important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T17:07:19-08:00","id":51987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=50609#post50609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just going to go back and reiterate that when you get all excessively wanky about how disease works, you probably wind up with something that doesn't function the least bit like disease in real life, and that both removes a lot of the resonance, and a lot of the actual relevant implications of disease in play.<br /> <br /> I mean, when cholera is called the besieging army's bane in First Edition, that's kind of an implication that if you have your army of tens of thousands of people squat down in the same place for months on end, their local water supply is going to get mixed up with their toilets, and that's going to leave them ravaged by disease.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point, and I don't want to sound like I'm being dismissive, but first, that's stuff from First Edition, which as far as I'm aware isn't necessarily relevant or correct in 2nd or 3E. So I'm hesitant to involve stuff from 1st Ed. And second, since when did people turn into wolves and/or summon hundreds of obsidian butterflies from their hand to mince their enemies in real life?<br /> <br /> But onto your main point. I'd say there that the problem isn't a conceptualisation of disease functioning or anything then, it's just being 'excessively wanky' as you put it. And that can spoil any aspect of the game. You can start arguing about how the Lunar changing thing doesn't conform with the conservation of mass/energy, or how changing like that should kill the person before they can finish, or how the Sid ability to 'have never been here but was' interacts with the general difficulty of teleportation in Creation. They're contrivances to facilitate gameplay and fun, and the books treatment of disease is inherently ambiguous anyway. So maybe the main problem isn't that it does/doesn't make sense, but that we have conflicting information. So, the real question we should be asking, rather than &quot;is this allowed/do bacteria and viruses exist?&quot;, is &quot;which rulebook am I saying has precedence over which other rulebook in the case of conflicts?&quot; Some treat disease as being mystical, which is fine. Others treat it as more biological, which is also fine. But Exalted, being the game that it is, will more or less inevitably deal with disease at some point in some way, so I guess the ST needs to make the best decision for his group and the story he wants to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:11:41-08:00","id":53402,"title":"","content":"Plant people, you say?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://postimg.org/image/4gug7rehp/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/4gug7rehp/zhaan.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/h38q1qmfx/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/67hc6e1i5/i_backed_ex3_small.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2045-melonlord82","name":"melonlord82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2045_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:27:38-08:00","id":53412,"title":"","content":"I never got around to saying it, but I think that when it comes to plant and fungus people, I prefer the sentient human shaped plants from the bonus East stuff to humans with mutations in a manner analogous to beastfolk. The pineys and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:31:21-08:00","id":53417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=51987#post51987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point, and I don't want to sound like I'm being dismissive, but first, that's stuff from First Edition, which as far as I'm aware isn't necessarily relevant or correct in 2nd or 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e stuff is highly relevant to 3e stuff, in that we love 1e stuff's tone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:35:30-08:00","id":53420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=51987#post51987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point, and I don't want to sound like I'm being dismissive, but first, that's stuff from First Edition, which as far as I'm aware isn't necessarily relevant or correct in 2nd or 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>First Edition is generally considered to have more credibility, and Third Edition will be more strongly building off of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And second, since when did people turn into wolves and/or summon hundreds of obsidian butterflies from their hand to mince their enemies in real life?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is always a terrible argument, but in this case is particularly distracting.<br /> <br /> It's not about the actual mechanism of disease, it's about how disease needs to work like disease actually works to retain resonance.<br /> <br /> This is like if the Guild didn't work by economics but by praying to generate responses from the Order-Conferring Trade Pattern the way people speculated the first time it was mentioned in Masters of Jade previewing and mocked in the actual book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:40:52-08:00","id":53422,"title":"","content":"Hey, Marst made a lot of money in the early days by looking for economic entities that showed signs of still trying to work the Trade Pattern, and scamming the fuck out of them based on known economic failure points likely to appear in models designed for a functional Trade Pattern but operating without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 01-19-2014, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:00:57-08:00","id":53434,"title":"","content":"Somewhere in Creation there's an army that thought they'd be a-okay when they set up siege if they just kept goats and criminals out of their water supply.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, they're spared the embarrassment of anybody knowing about it because they all died of cholera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:05:02-08:00","id":53438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=53434#post53434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somewhere in Creation there's an army that thought they'd be a-okay when they set up siege if they just kept goats and criminals out of their water supply.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, they're spared the embarrassment of anybody knowing about it because they all died of cholera.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am imagining a soldier running at full sprint to tackle an indigenous wild goat before it can reach the nearby stream, and receiving a hearty congratulations from his brothers-in-arms after he succeeds in scaring the long-bearded beast away. Later, they all die horribly of shitting themselves to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:07:48-08:00","id":53441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=53438#post53438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am imagining a soldier running at full sprint to tackle an indigenous wild goat before it can reach the nearby stream, and receiving a hearty congratulations from his brothers-in-arms after he succeeds in scaring the long-bearded beast away. Later, they all die horribly of shitting themselves to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:44:52-08:00","id":53473,"title":"","content":"I can't breathe... I can't breathe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T15:42:03-08:00","id":53517,"title":"","content":"If you somehow manage a hybrid between a virus and a human . . . you'd get a pretty normal human. After all, a reasonable portion of your DNA is the result of retroviruses infecting one of your ancestors and writing itself into that ancestor's chromosomes. <br /> <br /> It's not just a relic of ancient prehistory, either. Cattle in the Southwest US and rattlesnakes have a common chunk of DNA that is probably a result of a retrovirus that infected one and was transmitted to the other, the virus writing itself into the hereditary genome of both species. Had to happen some time in the last 500 years or so, since the rattlesnakes and cattle wouldn't have been in contact until then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T18:41:26-08:00","id":53618,"title":"","content":"Hey here's a thought on the whole &quot;occult versus realistic&quot; debate of disease: Why aren't they <i>both</i> true? <br /> <br /> Pissed off spirits can will germs into being from motes, and insert them into people they feel responsible for their difficulties. If placated, they can order the germs to die just as easily.<br /> <br /> Of course, the problem with this approach is that it spawns disease gods sooner or later, who can countermand the order if entrenched enough, and interfere with attempts to placate until then. Hence, why more conventional medicine exists, as disease gods can't do squat about that, it's literally hardwired into them out of Primordials Having Some Degree of Common Sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:26:16-08:00","id":53659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=53618#post53618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey here's a thought on the whole &quot;occult versus realistic&quot; debate of disease: Why aren't they <i>both</i> true?<br /> <br /> Pissed off spirits can will germs into being from motes, and insert them into people they feel responsible for their difficulties. If placated, they can order the germs to die just as easily.<br /> <br /> Of course, the problem with this approach is that it spawns disease gods sooner or later, who can countermand the order if entrenched enough, and interfere with attempts to placate until then. Hence, why more conventional medicine exists, as disease gods can't do squat about that, it's literally hardwired into them out of Primordials Having Some Degree of Common Sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, as we already discussed up-thread, it's rather messy and invites punching as prophylaxis and cure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:24:07-08:00","id":53969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=53659#post53659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because, as we already discussed up-thread, it's rather messy and invites punching as prophylaxis and cure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I didn't see that. Seriously, I skipped a lot of the thread.<br /> <br /> And in any case, killing the disease gods is only a temporary solution, at best. Their domain is still around, and will spawn a new god sooner or later. The best way to get rid of disease gods is to starve them, ie cure the disease conventionally.<br /> <br /> And if you're punching the source...the god still needs to be alive to call off the contagion, and if you force him, he's liable to start it up again all over out of spite as soon as your back is turned.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:38:13-08:00","id":53976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=53438#post53438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am imagining a soldier running at full sprint to tackle an indigenous wild goat before it can reach the nearby stream, and receiving a hearty congratulations from his brothers-in-arms after he succeeds in scaring the long-bearded beast away. Later, they all die horribly of shitting themselves to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gosh, I want draw this so badly it hurt !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:09:25-08:00","id":53999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=53969#post53969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I didn't see that. Seriously, I skipped a lot of the thread.<br /> <br /> And in any case, killing the disease gods is only a temporary solution, at best. Their domain is still around, and will spawn a new god sooner or later. The best way to get rid of disease gods is to starve them, ie cure the disease conventionally.<br /> <br /> And if you're punching the source...the god still needs to be alive to call off the contagion, and if you force him, he's liable to start it up again all over out of spite as soon as your back is turned.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the Immaculate Order has quite a successful track record in threatening gods to do what they want. Other Exalted would likely have a similar capacity to shove gods around through violence, or even talking. Talking down a plague is just as bad as being able to stop it by punching it in the face. That's not how you deal with epidemics - you get an expert in medical matters and get what you need for medical supplies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T10:02:10-08:00","id":54067,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that the Realm isn't free of epidemics thanks to the Immaculate Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T11:04:43-08:00","id":54095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/45674-beastmen-how-about-plantmen-fungusmen-or-virusmen-lunar-questions?p=53999#post53999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, the Immaculate Order has quite a successful track record in threatening gods to do what they want. Other Exalted would likely have a similar capacity to shove gods around through violence, or even talking. Talking down a plague is just as bad as being able to stop it by punching it in the face. That's not how you deal with epidemics - you get an expert in medical matters and get what you need for medical supplies.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Hm.<br /> <br /> Actually, this is a good reason to have both shamanism and scientific medicine being both extant disciplines in Creation. Punching works great some of the time, talking works great some of the time, and scientific medicine is grueling, dangerous labor...that works great all of the time. It's not playing with risks that the responsible spirits are mindless, or aren't going to listen to fists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T11:11:58-08:00","id":54103,"title":"","content":"I wonder how much sooner this thread would have died if I had not added virusmen as an afterthought in the original post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join D